WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:00.700
Joining us

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.334
now, Republican

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.068
Congressman Ken

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.803
Buck from Colorado,

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:07.140
who has voted for McCarthy so far.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.710
Congressman Buck, thanks for joining us.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.613
You said something to Kevin McCarthy

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:17.017
about what needs to happen going forward.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.785
Tell us what you said.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.186
Well, I've had a number of conversations

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:20.620
with Kevin,

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.921
and I've just basically told him

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:22.722
that at some point

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.157
this needs to break loose.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.092
He either needs to make a deal

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:29.362
to bring the 19 or 20 over or

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:30.964
he needs to step aside

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:31.731
and give somebody else

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:32.565
a chance to do that.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.601
I don't know what that timeframe is,

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:35.602
but it makes sense

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:36.269
that at some point

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.170
today, we

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.539
we are able to move forward in a way that

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.207
we elect a speaker.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.575
Unfortunately, the Democrats

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.109
won't agree

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.177
to a motion to adjourn

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.880
so that Republicans can meet the rebels.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.248
The 20 group

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.449
that that is opposing

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.417
McCarthy won't agree

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.851
to a motion to adjourn.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.719
So we're going to keep going

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.020
through this exercise on the floor.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.255
The smart thing to do is to

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.457
get together,

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:57.690
have a

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.925
conversation, choose

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:02.028
somebody and let's move forward.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:02.629
Right.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.597
I mean, one would have thought that

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.899
that would have happened already.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:06.332
It's not like

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.200
it was a mystery

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.435
that this vote was coming up

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:08.968
and somehow

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.004
Kevin McCarthy was caught unawares.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.506
I mean, we knew this vote was happening.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:14.841
And it seemed very clear

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.576
that whether it was five votes

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.644
or 20 votes,

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.344
Kevin McCarthy

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.513
was not going to have the votes.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.815
Do you think he's going to lose on this

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:23.083
fifth ballot?

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.217
Well, of course,

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:24.884
of course the

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.352
the 20 have not budged

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.253
and the Democrats

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.021
are going to vote for him.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.622
So we're pretty much going

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.723
to get the same vote

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.959
this time as we got the last four time.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.694
So your message to

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:35.862
Kevin McCarthy is basically

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.730
we need to fish or cut bait. We need to.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.501
If you can't get to 218 or 217,

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.536
whatever the threshold is,

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.338
we need to find someone else.

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:46.773
Who might that be?

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:46.873
Well,

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.241
I think the next in line is Steve

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.142
Scalise,

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:49.676
and I don't know

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.644
if Steve gets more or less.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.345
I think that

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.079
at some point

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:55.782
we've got to start looking at the rules

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.184
and the committee assignments

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:58.952
and other things

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.554
and just get back to the basics

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.555
of what people

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.357
what their self-interest is in this case

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.292
and meet some of those interests

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.161
and hopefully get the votes

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.263
Hey, Congressman, it's Dana Bash.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.665
Are you confident that if Steve Scalise

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.134
were nominated,

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:16.603
that he would be palatable to

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.438
enough of the 20

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:20.807
who won't vote for Kevin McCarthy?

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.442
So I think you need to break the 20 down.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.576
There are a few of those 20

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:24.377
that just aren't going to vote

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.211
for Kevin McCarthy,

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.546
but would vote for somebody else.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:27.480
There are some of the others

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.381
in that 20

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.183
who want changes in the rules

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:30.984
and there are some others

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.418
that care about policy.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.187
And so I think if Steve meets

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.655
those three needs

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:37.056
he will be able to move forward

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.759
and take the speakership.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:41.461
And Congressman Buck,

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.096
this is Abby Phillip.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.664
Thanks for being here.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.900
My question is about what you just said

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.034
about the timing of this.

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.802
You said that by today

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.337
you need to see some indication

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.173
of where this is going to go.

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.874
Do you think that by today

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.110
Kevin McCarthy needs to make that deal

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.479
or make a decision to move

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:01.548
out of the speaker's race?

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:03.183
I think at some point today,

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.684
the conference as a whole

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:05.785
needs to make a decision.

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.520
I think what's what's happening right now

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.622
is people are getting worn down.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:10.657
You're starting to get

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:12.992
some conflict,

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:13.793
open conflict

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:14.394
on the floor

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.196
as well as behind closed doors.

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:17.864
I think that conflict isn't healthy.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:19.399
And I think,

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:22.268
you know, the moderates are talking about

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.337
threats that they may work

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.372
with the Democrats on somebody

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.808
the 20 are saying that they're not moving

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:29.909
no matter what.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.711
At some point, people have to realize

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.246
that we've got to choose a speaker

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.147
and move forward.

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.848
The American people sent us here

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.016
to get the work done.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.818
Do you think Kevin McCarthy is hearing

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:39.385
your message?

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.821
Is he willing to step aside

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:44.123
if he loses on a fifth vote,

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.326
on a six vote on a seventh vote?

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:48.761
He's been preparing and hoping for this

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:49.429
his whole life.

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:49.963
His argument

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:50.530
might be, look,

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.564
I still have more votes

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.199
than any other Republican,

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:54.734
although certainly not more votes

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.135
than any one else running

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:56.703
because Hakeem

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.504
Jeffries keeps beating him.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.673
Do you sense any willingness to,

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:03.109
in your view, face the music?

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.711
Well, look, Hakeem Jeffries is losing

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.412
also Let's be honest,

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:07.247
there isn't a winner

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.048
until somebody gets in to 18.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.149
I just think he has more votes,

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:10.850
that's all.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.051
He has more votes,

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.487
but he doesn't have the ability

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:16.489
to become speaker in this Congress.

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:17.790
So Kevin McCarthy,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.691
I think,

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.326
will make the decision at some point.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.661
And what's going to happen

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.463
and what what should happen sooner

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:24.230
rather than later

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.832
is some of the senior members,

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.767
some of the cardinals on appropriations,

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:28.968
the committee chairmen,

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:29.802
some of the other folks

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:30.303
that have been here

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:31.938
a long time, have supported

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:33.606
Kevin, are going to have to have

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.141
that private conversation with them

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.242
that it doesn't make sense

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:37.710
and we need to move forward.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.978
Do you have any sense, sir,

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.514
that that's actually going to happen?

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:44.317
I have a sense it's common sense,

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:47.220
but I don't have a sense that it is.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.721
No one has whispered in my ear

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:49.689
that it's about that.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:50.923
Well, you've seen

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:51.991
what's been happening on the floor.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.459
I think common sense

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.961
left the room a while ago.

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.763
But just real quick,

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.665
I want to follow up on the comment

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:00.033
that you made about Steve Scalise.

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.000
You told Manu Raju

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.969
and you're saying now that he is

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:04.771
probably the

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.272
consensus candidate,

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.941
what would he need to do to get.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:11.077
I realize the 20 should be splitting

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:13.946
into various camps, but at the end

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.515
he would need to 18.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:16.983
How would he have to

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.584
what would he have to do to get that?

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:21.187
So I think that what Steve needs to do is

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:22.555
we have to have a break

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:23.623
whether it's this evening

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:24.557
or at some point.

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.225
And I think Steve just needs to sit down

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:27.493
with each individual,

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:28.828
talk to them about what they want.

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:29.829
Now, the problem is once

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:31.030
you make a commitment

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.032
to a conservative in the caucus,

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.133
then there's going to be a moderate

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:35.134
who says, wait a second,

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:35.902
I've been waiting for that

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:36.869
committee chairmanship

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:37.770
and I've been waiting for that

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.172
subcommittee chairmanship.

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:42.909
And so it is it's almost a zero sum game.

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:44.110
You start giving to one

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.611
side, you're taking away from the other.

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:47.313
Congressman Buck,

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:47.880
before you go,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.648
one last question,

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:50.083
which is how many votes do you think is

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:53.119
enough for this process to go on assuming

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:55.021
that Kevin McCarthy continues

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:56.122
to lose votes,

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:57.857
which he has been in the last few votes?

00:05:57.857 --> 00:06:00.126
I mean, this is the Fifth right now.

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.094
What's the maximum

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:03.329
you think would be acceptable all before?

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.365
There's a step to try

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:06.332
to find somebody else

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.401
that that will get to 17 or to 18.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:09.302
So if I knew

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:11.304
that I would be on a flight to Vegas

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:12.305
and I'd be putting my money

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:14.874
down on the table, I have no idea.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.509
I think it's going to be in the next two

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:20.079
or three votes that the nerves are frayed

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:20.613
enough

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:21.647
that people come together

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.082
and make a decision

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:24.350
And are you going to continue

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:25.351
voting for McCarthy,

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:26.552
or is your vote

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.121
possibly going to shift

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:29.188
to a different candidate?

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:32.058
If it's Steve Scalise or a present vote

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:33.626
Yeah.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.461
So I am voting on this vote

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.896
for Kevin McCarthy.

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:37.497
Stay tuned

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:38.398
and I'll let you know

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:40.166
what I'm going to be doing in the future.

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:40.500
All right.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.901
So this is the last time he can count

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:42.668
on your vote.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.070
This ballot right now, the fifth one.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.438
Congressman Ken Buck,

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:46.472
Colorado, thank you so much.

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:48.341
Really appreciate your time.

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:50.309
Good luck to you and your caucus of.

